# Environment Variables

Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your values.

```env
# ─── Application ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public URL of your Pulse instance (no trailing slash)
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Strong random secret for session signing
# Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=change-me-to-a-strong-random-secret

# ─── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SQLite (default — no setup needed, file is created automatically)
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# PostgreSQL (uncomment and fill in to use instead)
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/pulse?schema=public"

# ─── Optional: pre-seed Admin Account ────────────────────────────────────────
# If set, a user with this email/password is created on first run via the
# seeding script. Leave blank to register manually via the UI.
# SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
# SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=changeme
```

> **Note:** SMTP, Discord Webhook, and Cloudflare Edge Probe settings are
> managed through the Settings page in the dashboard — no `.env` changes needed.
